cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If this software, or the pixel-purity method it implements, is useful in your
  work, an acknowledgement is appreciated. Please cite it as below.
type: software
title: "Reading a Drought from Space: PSF-weighted grassland condition and cut detection from Sentinel-2"
abstract: >-
  A remote-sensing pipeline for the 2026 drought in the Canton of St. Gallen.
  It builds a point-spread-function-weighted pixel purity mask over a
  persistence-filtered parcel set, derives season NDMI trajectories and
  per-field anomalies per management type from swissEO S2-SR (Sentinel-2), and
  detects grassland cuts with a detector scored against hand labels. It runs
  end to end on synthetic data, so no restricted input data is needed to
  reproduce the pipeline.
authors:
  - family-names: Löw
    given-names: Fabian
repository-code: "https://github.com/floew2/drought-from-space-switzerland"
